@startuml trn-c4-container
' C4 Container — TRN (trn-service)
title TRN — Containers

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "trn-service\n(Spring Boot, Java 21, :8089)" as TRN
database "PostgreSQL\n(schema trn, per-tenant +\nneuroassist_global authority seeds)" as PG
database "Blob storage\n(voice samples / audio,\nper-subject crypto key)" as BLOB
database "Elasticsearch\n(approved-content index)" as ES

rectangle "Anthropic Claude" as LLM
rectangle "ElevenLabs" as TTS
rectangle "ACS (:8081)" as ACS
rectangle "PAT (:8082)" as PAT
rectangle "HIST (:8083)" as HIST
rectangle "CONV (:8085)" as CONV
rectangle "Eureka / REG (:8761)" as REG
rectangle "MIG (Flyway)" as MIG

TRN --> PG : JPA (schema-per-tenant);\noutbound_job durable-retry queue
TRN --> BLOB : voice samples + synthesized audio
TRN --> ES : SearchIndexPort (approved-only)
TRN --> LLM : LlmDialogPort (minimised context)
TRN --> TTS : TtsPort (consent-gated)
TRN --> ACS : JWKS validation; service-client token
TRN --> PAT : Feign — pat.patient.read (ETag/304)
TRN --> HIST : Feign — hist.audit.record
TRN --> CONV : Feign — publish / retire / erase\n(idempotent trn:publish:<approvalId>)
TRN ..> REG : register / discover
MIG ..> PG : applies trn migrations (V0080-V0089)

note bottom of TRN
  Messaging disabled: no broker. Resilience for long/flaky vendor and
  CONV calls = in-service durable-retry jobs (outbound_job), not a bus (ADR-007).
end note
@enduml
